# Images go through Git LFS rather than being stored as plain blobs, so `web/`'s assets are
# pointers and the bytes stay out of the packfile every clone downloads. A blob committed
# without this stays in history at full size even after the file is deleted, and only a
# history rewrite gets it back out. Audio is not listed here because it does not belong in
# the repository at all; see .gitignore.
*.png filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
*.jpg filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
*.jpeg filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
*.webp filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text

# Test fixtures are exempt, and the size argument above is the reason: an image small enough
# to be a fixture costs nothing in the packfile. It also has to be readable without LFS at
# all, because `actions/checkout` does not fetch LFS objects, so a fixture stored as a pointer
# reaches CI as pointer text and the test that decodes it fails only there.
**/tests/fixtures/*.png -filter -diff -merge -text
**/tests/fixtures/*.jpg -filter -diff -merge -text
**/tests/fixtures/*.jpeg -filter -diff -merge -text
**/tests/fixtures/*.webp -filter -diff -merge -text
